{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["But his bow remained taut — the strong bow that is called *albalestra* (crossbow), they mount it on a sturdy, strong piece of wood that is called *forka* (stock), and he who draws that bow, if he is a very strong man, draws the bowstring with his arms and his arms bend back against his body and he shoots the arrow far. And if he is weak he cannot draw the string. And so the meaning of the verses is: the Egyptians shot arrows at him and put him in prison, and afflicted his foot with fetters — yet he went out and ruled over them, because his bow was stronger and sturdier than theirs, and he bound them, as written: לאסור שריו בנפשו." "And the arms of his hands were made supple — his arms bent as he drew the bowstring and loosed his arrows against them, for he was a strong man, to draw the sturdy bow that is called *forka*. And so we find 'zeroa' (arm) in connection with drawing a bow, as written: ונחתה קשת נחושה זרועתי — and that is the language of drawing a bow. And likewise: כי חציך נחתו בי. And: ותנחת עלי ידיך." "Were made supple — were bent. Like: ויהי דוד מפזז ומכרכר. *Pizuz* is with the hands; *kirkur* is with the legs. And ויפוזו is from פזז, just as יסובו is from סבב." "From the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob — through the Holy One, blessed be He, this victory and dominion came to him." "The Mighty One of Jacob — a duplication of the construct form 'of'." "The Shepherd, the Rock of Israel — and likewise: אביר הרועים אשר לשאול — and the shepherds too are called אבירים, because the cattle and the bulls are called אבירים, as written: עדת אבירים בעגלי עמים. And likewise: סבבוני פרים רבים אבירי בשן כתרוני." "From the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob — What caused this for you? The Holy One, blessed be He, who is the Mighty One of Jacob, האלהים הרועה אותי עד היום הזה — for through His greatness He sustained me in Egypt." "From there — the Holy One, blessed be He, caused it to be." "The Shepherd, the Rock of Israel — the family of Israel, whom Yoseph sustained — his father and his brothers. אבן is a term for father and family. The nun is superfluous, like the nun of שגעון and עורון. And the mem of ריקם. And תהי הכנם."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The Old French loanwords *albalestra* (crossbow) and *forka* (stock/tiller) are retained in transliteration as Rashbam's technical terminology.", 8 "The phrase תהי הכנם appears textually uncertain; rendered hyper-literally without resolving."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:58.811567399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}